\f0\fs30 \cf0 Hexagonal Architecture :- Ports and Adapters Pattern Explain\
\
Course Details\
\
	This one-day training introduces Hexagonal Architecture (also known as the Ports & Adapters pattern). In this class, you will learn the core concepts through simple TypeScript examples and hands-on exercises. Although the code examples are intentionally small and easy to understand, the ideas behind them can significantly influence how you design applications and systems at a larger scale.\
\
	The training is not limited to small code snippets. We will also discuss application structure, the differences between layered architecture and modular architecture, and how the Hexagonal approach can help organize complex systems more effectively. In addition, we will explore practical strategies for migrating distributed architectures from a modular monolith.\
\
	Please bring your own laptop with any operating system capable of running TypeScript and Visual Studio Code. Questions are always welcome during the class \'97 including questions about using AI tools in development.\
